  "id": "COMPOUND:23096 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) is implicated in the biological pathway leading to CX-1 through multiple indirect mechanisms. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by several other molecules, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and Dendocarbin K. These intermediates ultimately target CX-1, indicating a complex network of interactions where Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) serves as a precursor or activator in the pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) in modulating the activity of CX-1 through the activation of SNU-387, which may exert its effects via a distinct mechanism. The evidence supports a link between the compound and CX-1 through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
